While I started playing the game with version 3.1.3, as near as I can
tell the game really hasn't changed that much since 3.1.  Before then,
there was no Marduk or Molloch, Gehennom was still called "Hell,"
there were fewer special levels and no Home dungeon, the Wiz still had
the Amulet, and the endgame was one level instead of five.  (This
information provided from memory from reading the old 3.0 spoilers.) 
Among the major changes since 3.1 (this is by no means exhaustive, and
someone else will have to point out the versions in which they
happened):

- New monsters: Chickatrices, Pyrolisks, Master Mind Flayers, Arch
Liches, Gas Spores, Green Slime, a horse pet progression and available
default pet.  (Also: Skeletons and Shades?)
- Mind Flayers (and Master Mind Flayers) and Scrolls of Amnesia
unidentify items.  (My least favorite change.)
- Roles: Monks and Rangers added to the game.  Elves (as a role)
removed.
- Races: separated from role.  Added: elves, dwarves, gnomes, orcs.
- Dungeon: Sokoban added to the game.
- Items: Amulets of Unchanging, Cornuthaums, Dunce Hats, Landmines
untrappable and as tool, Beartraps untrappable and as tool, Potions of
Polymorph, Scrolls of Earth, T-shirts, Flintstones, Touchstones (and
intrinsic gem ID removes from archelogists).
- Dungeon features: Graves.
- Dungeon rooms: Leprechaun halls, Antholes, Cockatrice nests, Swamp
levels, probably one or two others I'm forgetting.
- The lighting store in minetown, and its honored proprietor.
- Polypiling produces golems a lot more often.
- More minetowns and mineends.
- Game features: Alchemy, Weapon Skills, Bare-handed Fighting Skill,
Magic Skills, Two-Weapon Combat ability and skill, a Quivver, a
favored spell for each class, steeds and riding.

Can anyone date these additions, and add more?

